<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Close</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>close &lt;item&gt;
close &lt;door&gt;
close &lt;direction&gt; &lt;door&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>close coffin
close door
close south gate
</pre>
<p>Closes something that can be opened and closed: a chest, a bag, a coffin, 
or a door, gate or hatch on the way out of a room. Doors are named by a 
keyword, such as door or gate; if there are several, add the direction. 
Closing a door closes it on both sides, and those on the other side see it 
close.
</p><p>You can also close something you are inside, such as a coffin, from the 
inside. You can close things while sitting or resting, but not asleep.
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Open</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Lock</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Unlock</a>
</pre>




</div>